    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**Verification of the produced id** (from the audit log): `NSW2616E6609E3` \u2014 `NSW` (region) + `26` (FY) + `16E6609E` (HASH8) + `3` (Luhn CHK over the digits of `NSW2616E6609E`).\n\n### Changes made\n\n**Model & persistence**\n- `Owner.java`: replaced the `customer_code`/`customerCode` field, getter, and setter with `member_id`/`memberId`.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`: renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` (widened to hold the longer id).\n\n**API contract**\n- `openapi.yml`: removed the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties; added `memberId` with the new format; updated the `fiscalYear` and `locality` descriptions to reference the memberId. (The `OwnerDto` is regenerated from this spec.)\n\n**Controller (`OwnerRestControllerV1`)**\n- Replaced `customerCode(owner)` with `memberId(owner)`, which builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` \u2014 region from postcode/city, FY from the fiscal-year segment, HASH8 = same SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) first-8-hex, and CHK = Luhn over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n- Collision handling (`deduplicate`) now applies to `memberId`.\n- `primaryIdentifier` and the human-readable audit line now reference `memberId`; the audit line no longer emits the removed fields.\n\n**Mapper (`OwnerMapper`)**\n- Removed the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings and methods (and the now-unused `Luhn` import).\n- `locality` now reads the REGION segment from `memberId` (matching the known region prefix, since the format is separator-less), with the same fallback to `Region.code`.\n- `fiscalYear` now reads its FY segment from `memberId` (with a registration-date fallback for seed data).\n\n**Audit event (`OwnerCreatedEvent`)**\n- Renamed the identifier component from `customerCode` to `memberId`, so the structured JSON audit record now carries `\"memberId\"`.\n\nDoc comments in `Sha256Hasher` and `Luhn` were updated to reflect the new id.",
